  "origin": "PROTOTYPE record demonstrating a proposed solution to Gap C (large distributed creator population). Same source as pleias-common-corpus-youtube-commons.jsonld but with a creator manifest reference. The originator entry carries a `manifest` field pointing at a separate CreatorManifest document (examples/prototypes/pleias-common-corpus-youtube-commons-creator-manifest.jsonld) that lists/excerpts the 721,136 individual YouTube channels. This lets the record point at a checkable roster rather than compressing 721k creators into one prose name. NOTE: the `manifest` field is NOT part of the 0.0.1 schema — this record will NOT validate against the current schema as-is; it is intentionally a forward-looking prototype. See notes/stress-test-pleias-common-corpus.md (Gap C proposed direction).",
